", "updated_at": "2026-09-21T12:32:38Z", "actor": {"login": "artf", "id": 11614725, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExNjE0NzI1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11614725?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf", "html_url": "https://github.com/artf", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "run_attempt": 1, "referenced_workflows": [], "run_started_at": "2026-09-21T12:30:56Z", "triggering_actor": {"login": "artf", "id": 11614725, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExNjE0NzI1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11614725?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf", "html_url": "https://github.com/artf", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/artf/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "jobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/runs/35599979423/jobs", "logs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/runs/35599979423/logs", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/check-suites/96381354336", "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/runs/35599979423/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/runs/35599979423/cancel", "rerun_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/runs/35599979423/rerun", "previous_attempt_url": null, "workflow_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GrapesJS/grapesjs/actions/workflows/113825841", "head_commit": {"id": "857dd0f49f6dc850799e08a133cf23b31a9cbda5", "tree_id": "9679da429e34bf03ab0621d46a0d94159fa9ffd2", "message": "fix: drag&drop issues when the editor is in a shadowRoot (#6824)\n\n* fix(sorter): keep the placeholder attached when the editor is in a shadow root\n\nSorter#ensurePlaceholderElement re-appended the placeholder to\ncontainerContext.container whenever `!el.ownerDocument.contains(el)`. `Node.contains`\nwalks the node tree without crossing shadow boundaries, so for an editor mounted in\na shadow root the guard always answered \"not attached\" \u2014 the placeholder element is\n`Canvas#getPlacerEl()`, which lives in the tools layer, i.e. in the host page DOM.\n\nEvery placeholder move therefore ripped it out of the tools layer and injected it\ninto the container, which for the canvas sorters is the iframe body (Droppable,\nSelectPosition and BlocksView all pair `getPlacerEl()` with the canvas body). The\nGrapesJS stylesheet is not loaded there, so the placeholder became invisible.\n\nFix: test `el.isConnected`, the shadow-aware equivalent, which behaves identically\noutside shadow DOM.\n\nIntroduced by the sorter refactor in #6149 (0.22.1). The previous implementation\nonly appended the placeholder when the `placer` option was absent, and the canvas\nsorters always passed it, so the append branch was never taken.\n\n* fix(sorter): hit-test against the container's root node so sorting works in a shadow root\n\nDropLocationDeterminer#getMouseTargetElement resolved the drop target with\n`containerContext.document.elementFromPoint()`. `Document.elementFromPoint` does\nnot pierce shadow boundaries, so when a sorter container lives inside a shadow\nroot it returned the shadow host instead of the hovered item. The subsequent\n`getFirstElementWithAModel` walk is bounded by\n`containerContext.container.contains(el)`, which is false for the host, so it\nreturned null and handleMove bailed out on every sample: no placeholder, no\ndrop, silent failure.\n\nThis hits the Layer Manager when rendered into the host page via\n`layerManager.appendTo` (ItemsView hardcodes `document: document`), making layer\nreordering a no-op. The canvas is unaffected because its containerContext\ndocument is the iframe document.\n\nFix: run the hit-test on `container.getRootNode()`, which is the ShadowRoot when\nthe container is in a shadow tree and the Document otherwise. `ShadowRoot`\nimplements the same DocumentOrShadowRoot mixin and resolves within its own tree,\nso behaviour outside shadow DOM is unchanged; the isFunction guard falls back to\ncontainerContext.document for a detached container.\n\nIntroduced by the sorter refactor in #6149 (0.22.1), which replaced the previous\n`e.target` lookup \u2014 not retargeted for a listener inside the same shadow tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Guillaume Fauvet <gfauvet@antidot.net>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>", "timestamp": "2026-09-21T12:30:52Z", "author": {"name": "fauvetg", "email": "gui.fauvet@gmail.com"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com"}}, "repository": {"id": 50146229, "node_id": "MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk1MDE0NjIyOQ==", "name": "grapesjs", "full_name": "Gra